    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="0831" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.90F/9</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 370</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-24">May 24, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State transmits for the information of and appropriate comment
                    by the American Minister Resident and Consul General <pb facs="0832" n="826"
                        xml:id="pg826"/> a copy of an instruction,<anchor n="6" xml:id="d867-f1"/>
                    with enclosure, addressed to the American Minister in Cairo concerning the
                    possible establishment of diplomatic or consular representation in Saudi
                    Arabia.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
